==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sent-|id=feel}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|cōnsēnsus||agreement, accordance, unanimity}}, from {{m|la|cōnsentiō||feel together; agree}}; see {{m|en|consent}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈsɛnsəs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-PerfectSoundWhatever-consensus.wav|Audio (CA)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|+|consensus}}

# A process of [[w:Group decision-making#Decision-making in social settings|decision-making]] that seeks widespread agreement among group members.
# [[general#Adjective|General]] agreement among the members of a given group or community, each of which exercises some [[discretion]] in decision-making and follow-up action.
#: {{co|en|reach '''consensus'''}}
#: {{ux|en|After years of debate over the best wine to serve at Thanksgiving, no real '''consensus''' has emerged.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} An [[agreement]] on some data value that is needed during [[computation]].
# {{lb|en|attributive}} Average projected value.
#: {{ux|en|a financial '''consensus''' forecast}}

